# Auto-merge policy

Merging a PR to `master` does NOT require asking the user when ALL of these hold:

- Local gates green on the head SHA — this repo has no working CI (org
  Actions billing is locked): the agent ran `npm test` + `npm run typecheck`
  inside `wise-fiskl-webhook/` on a checkout of the head. The kept
  `wise-fiskl-webhook.yml` workflow is advisory only; its pending/failed
  state from the billing lock is not signal.
- The pre-merge review gate in `AGENTS.md` is satisfied: all review threads
  resolved, bot-authored commits reviewed, gates re-run on the head SHA if
  it moved.
- No merge conflicts; head mergeable.

When all hold: merge to `master`, then `git pull` the updated base into
affected local checkouts. Report the merge in the summary.

Still ask first when: unresolved review findings, conflicts needing
non-trivial resolution, or the diff touches secrets/billing/destructive ops.
When unsure — ask.
